## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end security of hybrid AI platforms, spanning software supply chain and model governance, with practical incident response capabilities.

## Key Concepts
- Secure software supply chain and model governance
- SBOMs, image/model signing, and cryptographic attestations
- Provenance verification and reproducible builds
- Policy-as-Code enforcement with OPA Gatekeeper
- Runtime attestation in Kubernetes environments
- Data provenance tracking for training datasets
- Incident response playbooks and success metrics

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: sign an image with cosign
const { execSync } = require('child_process');

function signContainerImage(imageUrl) {
  // Generate SBOM
  execSync(`syft ${imageUrl} -o cyclonedx-json > sbom.json`);

  // Sign the image
  execSync(`cosign sign --key cosign.key ${imageUrl}`);

  // Attach SBOM as attestation
  execSync(`cosign attest --predicate sbom.json --type cyclonedx ${imageUrl}`);

  console.log(`Successfully signed ${imageUrl}`);
}
```

Why This Is Asked

This question tests defense-in-depth for multi-tenant data access with concrete controls, not abstract concepts.

Key Concepts

- Row-Level Security (RLS) in PostgreSQL to enforce tenant isolation at the data layer
- Per-tenant IAM roles and ephemeral credentials to limit data-plane access
- Open Policy Agent (OPA) policy enforcement at the gateway to block cross-tenant requests
- Service mesh mTLS isolation to protect service-to-service communication
- CI checks to catch misconfigurations and a detailed IR playbook with success criteria

Code Example

```javascript
// Example: basic tenant-bound check in Express middleware
function tenantGuard(req, res, next) {
  const tenantId = req.user?.tenant_id;
  const pathTenant = req.params?.tenantId;
  if (pathTenant && tenantId !== pathTenant) return res.status(403).send('Forbidden');
  next();
}
```

